      "message": "I think aosp/4368000 later in the chain undoes this patch: at the top of the chain `videobuf2-memops.c` and `videobuf2-memops.h` match their content before this patch, and `videobuf2-dma-contig.c` and `videobuf2-dma-sg.c` differ only in whitespace. Instead, it rejects USERPTR from 4KB processes with `-EOPNOTSUPP` in `videobuf2-core.c`.\n\nWould it be OK to drop this patch and move that rejection here? It only needs `mm_is_p3s_4k()` from `\u003clinux/p3s/mm.h\u003e`, so it should work at this point in the chain, and 4KB processes would get a clear error from the start.\n\nAs far as I can see, without this patch a 4KB process gets `-ENOSPC` from `get_vaddr_frames()` here, but only because of the frame vector part of aosp/4367611, which aosp/4368000 reverts as well.",
